The files in this directory are test data for the rates package's parser tests.

kraken.json, kraken-xmr.json, coinbase.json, yadio.json and bitfinex.json are recorded answers of the providers'
public APIs (Kraken's Ticker for BTC and for XMR, Coinbase's exchange rates and Yadio's exchange rates for BTC, and
Bitfinex's tickers for XMR/USD and its BTC pairs), with their response headers in the matching *.meta.json. They are
public market data of one instant, used only as parser fixtures. Kraken's and Coinbase's answers are trimmed to what
the tests read: Kraken's seven BTC fiat pairs (kraken.json) and its two XMR pairs (kraken-xmr.json), and Coinbase's
rates for those seven codes plus the code with the longest fraction when that is longer; Yadio's and Bitfinex's are
whole. TestLiveRecord (rates/live_test.go, build tag live) re-records and trims them; TestFixturesAreTrimmed checks
the committed files are trimmed. custom.json is written by hand in SatBooth's own format. ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS.md
credits the providers.
